A||||4||WisconsinGT||Did the Dickman steel vacuum lines||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||10-17-2000||01:13 AM||||Thought I would share my experience installing the lines. Overall it went extremely well. I found out I had two cracked lines. The steel lines from Rodney were (Much to my surprise) a perfect fit. I was amazed at how easy it was. Since I am not even close to being a shade tree mechanic, I would say that anyone can do this. The one problem that annoyed the hell out of me was getting the steel lines to fit/snap into the stock spacer things. After I bolted everything up I then realized that I should have taken the spacer things out. I am sure it would have done no harm. FWIW<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||10-17-2000||01:56 AM||||On his site it says they are not stainless.  What did you coat them with before installing them?  How much was it?<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||10-17-2000||07:19 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by WisconsinGT:<BR><B>Thought I would share my experience installing the lines. ... I found out I had two cracked lines. The steel lines from Rodney were (Much to my surprise) a perfect fit... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>No surprise to me. Rodney produces top quality stuff. You can tell he takes pride in what he does.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Just my $.02. Thanks for the space.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 10-17-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||Rodney||10-17-2000||10:01 AM||||My V-6 vacuum lines are mild steel. Stainless steel is too hard to work with and the price would be probably 4x more. I doubt I ever make them in stainless steel. One guy did have a set chrome plated so I will always have some sets available in uncoated steel for those people. They have to be painted. Early(?) next year I will have black zinc plated sets for $99. I will be making up maybe 50 sets which is about a 3 month job and getting them all plated which is a big job. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||StuGood||10-18-2000||08:49 AM||||Painting them sounds good.  That way, I can color code them.  Works for simple-minded people like myself  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 10-18-2000).]||||reg||10
